==============================================================================
(1) BAND-TRANSVERSAL T_p: tight sets + covering-min obey the SAME T_p, p<=23
==============================================================================
   AP    : T_p all hold p<=23? True   #gaps mod 14 = 2
   GW    : T_p all hold p<=23? True   #gaps mod 14 = 2
   C-min : T_p all hold p<=23? True   #gaps mod 14 = 2
   radii floor(p/14): [(2, 0), (3, 0), (5, 0), (7, 0), (11, 0), (13, 0), (17, 1), (19, 1), (23, 1)]
   => resonance-kill (p<14: 2,3,5,7,11,13) + transversal (14<=p<28: 17,19,23)

   NECESSARY-NOT-SUFFICIENT: prime-T_p (p<=23) counterexamples with 4 gaps are
   all NON-tight (deeper hole elsewhere):
     [1, 5, 6, 10, 11, 12, 15, 19, 20, 21, 23, 25, 26]: M=4/31  gaps=4  (tight? False)
     [4, 5, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 18, 19, 22, 23, 24, 26]: M=2/15  gaps=4  (tight? False)

==============================================================================
(2) CYCLE route: diff-closed tight = dilated AP = rotation orbit => Steinhaus
==============================================================================
   n= 5 c=1: residues=orbit; M=1/5 (=1/n? True) gaps=2 (Steinhaus <=3? True)
   n= 5 c=2: residues=orbit; M=1/5 (=1/n? True) gaps=2 (Steinhaus <=3? True)
