   n=11 c=2: residues=orbit; M=1/11 (=1/n? True) gaps=2 (Steinhaus <=3? True)
   n=13 c=1: residues=orbit; M=1/13 (=1/n? True) gaps=2 (Steinhaus <=3? True)
   n=13 c=2: residues=orbit; M=1/13 (=1/n? True) gaps=2 (Steinhaus <=3? True)
   n=14 c=1: residues=orbit; M=1/14 (=1/n? True) gaps=2 (Steinhaus <=3? True)

==============================================================================
(3) WIDE-HOLE/SUPPORT route: #gaps = 1 + #distinct-run-lengths(missing)
==============================================================================
   identity check on tight sets:
     AP: missing run-lengths=[1]  1+#distinct=2  actual gaps=2
     GW: missing run-lengths=[1]  1+#distinct=2  actual gaps=2
   => 4 gaps needs 3 distinct run-lengths => missing>=1+2+3=6 => support>=n-5 => <=3 gaps

   wide-hole bound (n=14): missing>=4 (support<=10) forces M>1/14:
     missing=4 (support=10): 8000 configs; M<=1/14: 0
     missing=5 (support=9): 8000 configs; M<=1/14: 0
     missing=6 (support=8): 8000 configs; M<=1/14: 0

NET: rigidity g(n)<=3 = Steinhaus on the rotation orbit-cycle (diff-closed exact)
     + support>=n-5 via the wide-hole inequality (general). T_p = common skeleton.
